From 7c925c45022887504a83f9760e79a192ec5f52e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amelia Crate <amelia.crate@chainguard.dev>
Date: Thu, 4 Dec 2025 15:17:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] crypto: reusable jitterentropy

Vendor sha3 for jitterentropy usage. In 6.12 we did this by managing SHA3 state
and calling sha3 functions directly but the SHA3 algorithm no longer implements
partial block handling but relies on the crypto API level partial block handling,
so this is no longer feasible.

* copy sha3_generic to sha3-jitterentropy
* shim function calls in certified sha3-jitterentropy
* move crypto algorithm registration and macros to a recompilable sha3-jitterentropy-kcapi object
* register algorithm on jitterentropy-kcapi startup
---
 crypto/jitterentropy-kcapi.c      |  10 +-
 crypto/jitterentropy-shim.c       |  10 ++
 crypto/jitterentropy-shim.h       |   2 +
 crypto/sha3-jitterentropy-kcapi.c |  43 ++++++
 crypto/sha3-jitterentropy.c       | 217 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 crypto/sha3_jitter.h              |  16 +++
 include/crypto/sha3_jitter.h      |  38 ++++++
 7 files changed, 334 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 crypto/sha3-jitterentropy-kcapi.c
 create mode 100644 crypto/sha3-jitterentropy.c
 create mode 100644 crypto/sha3_jitter.h
 create mode 100644 include/crypto/sha3_jitter.h

